1330
00:51:45.310 --> 00:51:48.930
He's saying, you know, the recruiter told me my eyes were too bad to enliSt.
他说，你知道吗，征兵人员说我的视力太差，不能参军。

1331
00:51:49.190 --> 00:51:50.330
Phyllis is like, I'm sorry.
菲利斯说，我很遗憾。

1332
00:51:50.330 --> 00:51:52.270
It sounds like you really wanted to go to Vietnam.
听起来你真的很想去越南。

1333
00:51:52.470 --> 00:51:53.650
Can I have some more of that brandy?
我还能再喝点那白兰地吗？

1334
00:51:54.050 --> 00:51:55.970
This is a ridiculous conversation.
这对话太荒谬了。

1335
00:51:56.210 --> 00:51:57.270
Stanley says, sure can.
斯坦利说，当然可以。

1336
00:51:57.270 --> 00:51:58.630
And don't call me brandy.
还有，别叫我白兰地。

1337
00:51:58.790 --> 00:51:59.790
And then they start laughing.
然后他们开始大笑。

1338
00:51:59.790 --> 00:52:03.670
And then Stanley goes to pour Phyllis a drink and it overflows.
接着斯坦利给菲利斯倒酒，结果倒溢出来了。

1339
00:52:04.150 --> 00:52:06.930
He says, whoops-a-daisy, Stanley's drunk.
他说，哎呀，斯坦利喝醉了。

1340
00:52:07.250 --> 00:52:11.370
And he looks at the spill and says, have you ever seen anything so sad?
他看着洒出来的酒说，你见过比这更悲惨的事吗？

1341
00:52:11.490 --> 00:52:12.290
And they laugh.
然后他们笑了。

1342
00:52:12.290 --> 00:52:15.750
And then Phyllis dabs a little bit of brandy behind her ear.
接着菲利斯在耳后抹了一点白兰地。

1343
00:52:16.670 --> 00:52:17.730
Where's this going?
这要往哪儿发展？

1344
00:52:17.990 --> 00:52:20.230
She says, this drives Bob crazy.
她说，这会让鲍勃疯狂的。

1345
00:52:20.950 --> 00:52:24.650
Then she starts wincing and goes, ow, ow, ow, my eczema.
然后她开始皱眉，说，哎哟，哎哟，哎哟，我的湿疹。

1346
00:52:24.990 --> 00:52:25.210
Ow.
哎哟。

1347
00:52:25.210 --> 00:52:26.950
He says, okay, it's better.
他说，好了，好点了吗。

1348
00:52:27.670 --> 00:52:28.810
Stanley goes, you okay?
斯坦利问，你还好吗？

1349
00:52:29.110 --> 00:52:31.350
And Phyllis says, yes, thank you for asking.
菲利斯说，是的，谢谢你的关心。

1350
00:52:32.090 --> 00:52:33.670
Stanley says, you are welcome.
斯坦利说，不客气。

1351
00:52:33.970 --> 00:52:35.810
I'm on the edge of my seat right now.
我现在紧张得坐立难安。

1352
00:52:35.990 --> 00:52:38.390
Then there is a long pause.
接着是一段长时间的停顿。

1353
00:52:38.810 --> 00:52:39.330
What?
什么？

1354
00:52:39.530 --> 00:52:43.330
And then here's something they say at the same time.
然后是他们同时说的一句话。

1355
00:52:44.270 --> 00:52:45.290
Overlapping dialogue.
重叠的对话。

1356
00:52:45.630 --> 00:52:49.850
Overlapping dialogue after a long pause and drinking brandy.
在长时间停顿和喝白兰地之后的重叠对话。

1357
00:52:50.970 --> 00:52:53.170
Stanley says, how's Bob doing?
斯坦利问，鲍勃怎么样了？

1358
00:52:54.010 --> 00:52:56.990
Phyllis says, I've never been with a black man before.
菲利斯说，我以前从没和黑人在一起过。

1359
00:52:57.390 --> 00:52:57.930
What?
什么？

1360
00:52:58.690 --> 00:52:59.230
What?
什么？

1361
00:52:59.810 --> 00:53:00.350
Wow.
哇。

1362
00:53:00.910 --> 00:53:03.450
And then there is a long beat.
然后又是一段长时间的沉默。

1363
00:53:03.770 --> 00:53:05.970
And Stanley says, good night.
接着斯坦利说，晚安。

1364
00:53:07.430 --> 00:53:11.190
And he leaves feeling a little awkward and exits.
他感到有点尴尬，然后离开了。

1365
00:53:11.510 --> 00:53:12.290
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1366
00:53:12.330 --> 00:53:13.530
There's so much to unpack.
这里面信息量太大了。

1367
00:53:13.830 --> 00:53:14.830
There is so much to unpack.
这里面信息量太大了。

1368
00:53:15.430 --> 00:53:19.670
Okay, so first of all, it answers the question, they have not hooked up before.
好吧，首先，这回答了那个问题，他们之前确实没搞在一起过。

1369
00:53:19.830 --> 00:53:20.790
They've never hooked up.
他们从来没搞在一起过。

1370
00:53:20.790 --> 00:53:25.650
But I feel like it sort of teases that in this moment, Phyllis might have.
但我感觉这一刻似乎暗示了菲利斯可能动过心。

1371
00:53:25.750 --> 00:53:26.890
Might have been up for it.
可能是有过那种想法。

1372
00:53:26.950 --> 00:53:27.330
Yes.
没错。

1373
00:53:27.530 --> 00:53:30.910
Is this her, I knew what I was doing, Pam moment?
这是她那种“我知道自己在做什么，帕姆”的时刻吗？

1374
00:53:31.070 --> 00:53:32.650
I think maybe so.
我觉得或许是吧。

1375
00:53:32.870 --> 00:53:37.330
And, you know, so many fan theories point to these moments where there was tenderness between them,
而且，你知道，很多粉丝理论都指向这些他们之间流露温情的时刻，

1376
00:53:37.450 --> 00:53:39.250
even though they got on each other's nerves.
尽管他们平时总是互相看不顺眼。

1377
00:53:39.430 --> 00:53:39.650
Yes.
是的。

1378
00:53:39.890 --> 00:53:43.830
You know, I mean, Stanley whittled that whole thing for her.
我是说，斯坦利为她雕刻了那个东西。

1379
00:53:44.070 --> 00:53:44.390
Phyllis.
菲利斯。

1380
00:53:44.550 --> 00:53:44.830
Yeah.
对。

1381
00:53:45.010 --> 00:53:45.850
As a chicken.
那个小鸡。

1382
00:53:46.090 --> 00:53:46.330
Yes.
是的。

1383
00:53:46.330 --> 00:53:46.790
Or whatever.
或者别的什么。

1384
00:53:47.030 --> 00:53:49.250
As a bird person in the finale.
大结局里那个鸟人形象。

1385
00:53:49.550 --> 00:53:51.190
I mean, he clearly cares for her.
我是说，他显然很在乎她。

1386
00:53:51.270 --> 00:53:51.430
Yeah.
是啊。

1387
00:53:52.170 --> 00:53:56.470
But, yeah, I'm telling you, the long pause is where everything happens.
但是，我跟你说，长时间的停顿才是关键所在。

1388
00:53:57.310 --> 00:53:58.590
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1389
00:53:58.730 --> 00:53:59.670
Put that on a mug.
把这句话印在马克杯上吧。

1390
00:54:00.770 --> 00:54:03.130
So there was my mom detective moment.
这就是我的“妈妈侦探”时刻。

1391
00:54:03.390 --> 00:54:04.230
I loved it.
我太喜欢了。

1392
00:54:04.430 --> 00:54:06.630
Thank you, Dave, for pointing me in the right direction.
谢谢你，戴夫，给我指明了方向。

1393
00:54:06.630 --> 00:54:12.010
But, yeah, I mean, a little bit of brandy, dot, dot, dot.
不过，我是说，喝点白兰地，点点点。

1394
00:54:12.630 --> 00:54:13.310
Dot, dot.
点点。

1395
00:54:13.610 --> 00:54:14.650
But nothing happened.
但什么都没发生。

1396
00:54:14.970 --> 00:54:19.190
And I think that settles it that they had never hooked up.
我觉得这足以证明他们从未搞在一起过。

1397
00:54:19.570 --> 00:54:23.090
Well, in real life, Leslie and Phyllis were very good friends.
嗯，在现实生活中，莱斯利和菲利斯是非常好的朋友。

1398
00:54:23.290 --> 00:54:24.650
They are still good friends.
他们现在依然是好朋友。

1399
00:54:24.790 --> 00:54:32.390
In fact, Leslie said his favorite person to do scenes with is Phyllis because she's an amazing actress and because they are friends in real life.
事实上，莱斯利说他最喜欢和菲利斯演对手戏，因为她是一位了不起的演员，而且他们现实中也是朋友。

1400
00:54:32.390 --> 00:54:37.750
And we reached out to Phyllis to ask her about working with Leslie, and she said this.
我们联系了菲利斯，问她关于和莱斯利合作的事，她是这么说的。

1401
00:54:38.430 --> 00:54:46.230
Leslie is a real stand-up guy with character and principles and a sense of humor that just adds charm and wit when being with him.
莱斯利是个真正光明磊落的人，有品格、有原则，而且幽默感十足，和他在一起总是充满魅力和风趣。

1402
00:54:46.890 --> 00:54:50.170
She confirmed that they did a lot of online shopping together.
她证实他们经常一起在网上购物。

1403
00:54:50.310 --> 00:54:56.570
And she said they would also run to Walmart and do errands together if there was ever a long break in filming.
她说如果拍摄间隙有较长的休息时间，他们还会一起跑去沃尔玛办杂事。

1404
00:54:56.930 --> 00:54:58.050
Could you imagine?
你能想象吗？

1405
00:54:58.430 --> 00:54:59.250
I know.
我知道。

1406
00:54:59.490 --> 00:54:59.950
I know.
我知道。

1407
00:54:59.950 --> 00:55:04.910
Like if they weren't in a couple of scenes in the afternoon, they'd just go hop over to Walmart together.
就像如果他们下午有几场戏没戏份，他们就会一起溜去沃尔玛。

1408
00:55:05.110 --> 00:55:05.910
It's so adorable.
太可爱了。

1409
00:55:06.490 --> 00:55:09.930
And they also would show up for each other at their premieres and things.
而且他们还会出席彼此的首映礼之类的活动。

1410
00:55:10.150 --> 00:55:15.850
I mean, I saw a picture that Leslie went with Phyllis for her, the OA, the show on Netflix, her premiere.
我是说，我看到一张照片，莱斯利陪菲利斯去了她的首映礼，就是网飞那部剧《先见之明》。

1411
00:55:16.090 --> 00:55:16.310
Yeah.
是啊。

1412
00:55:16.390 --> 00:55:17.850
He did the red carpet with her.
他陪她走了红毯。

1413
00:55:18.430 --> 00:55:21.230
But we all used to get paired up to do press on the show.
以前我们拍这部剧时，总是被安排成对去参加媒体宣传活动。

1414
00:55:21.450 --> 00:55:23.530
You know, I would get paired up with Brian or Rain.
你知道，我以前常和布莱恩或雷恩一组。

1415
00:55:23.690 --> 00:55:25.610
You would get paired up with John quite a bit.
你以前经常和约翰一组。

1416
00:55:25.710 --> 00:55:26.030
Usually.
通常是这样。

1417
00:55:26.270 --> 00:55:28.830
And Phyllis and Leslie were always paired up together.
而菲利斯和莱斯利总是被分在一起。

1418
00:55:28.830 --> 00:55:34.950
Rather, I found an interview of the two of them on the red carpet for the BAFTA tea years ago.
其实，我找到了他们俩多年前在英国电影学院奖茶会红毯上的一次采访。

1419
00:55:34.950 --> 00:55:39.470
So they were very excited about things that were coming up for their characters on the show.
当时他们对剧中角色即将迎来的剧情发展感到非常兴奋。

1420
00:55:39.570 --> 00:55:41.450
And I watched the whole interview.
我看了整个采访。

1421
00:55:41.450 --> 00:55:45.890
It just warmed my heart because you could just, I don't know, you could hear their love for the show.
这让我心里暖暖的，因为你可以，我不知道，你可以听出他们对这部剧的热爱。

1422
00:55:46.030 --> 00:55:48.250
You could hear their familiarity and friendship.
你可以听出他们的默契和友谊。

1423
00:55:48.510 --> 00:55:49.930
And I thought I'd share it.
所以我想分享一下。

1424
00:55:50.550 --> 00:55:50.990
Hello, sir.
你好，先生。

1425
00:55:51.050 --> 00:55:51.570
How are you doing?
你好吗？

1426
00:55:52.510 --> 00:55:53.650
Huge office freak.
我是《办公室》的超级剧迷。

1427
00:55:53.970 --> 00:55:54.070
All right.
好的。

1428
00:55:54.170 --> 00:55:54.390
Yes.
是的。

1429
00:55:54.550 --> 00:55:55.470
It's one of my favorite shows.
这是我最喜欢的剧之一。

1430
00:55:55.470 --> 00:55:57.030
Okay, what can we expect this year?
好的，今年我们可以期待些什么呢？

1431
00:55:57.310 --> 00:55:57.990
Well, we know.
嗯，我们都知道。

1432
00:55:58.190 --> 00:55:59.250
All the spoilers.
全是剧透。

1433
00:56:00.070 --> 00:56:03.010
Well, you already saw Thursday night what happened.
嗯，你周四晚上已经看到发生了什么了。

1434
00:56:03.210 --> 00:56:04.230
I have issues.
我有麻烦了。

1435
00:56:05.210 --> 00:56:05.550
I know.
我知道。

1436
00:56:05.690 --> 00:56:06.370
He's showing up.
他要出现了。

1437
00:56:06.450 --> 00:56:11.990
I'm cheating and tearing up cars and just, you know, I'm having a midlife man crisis.
我在出轨，在拆车，你知道的，我正在经历中年危机。

1438
00:56:11.990 --> 00:56:12.670
I don't know.
我不知道。

1439
00:56:12.930 --> 00:56:14.170
Are you happy with that storyline?
你对这个故事情节满意吗？

1440
00:56:14.850 --> 00:56:17.990
I am because it was so much fun to do.
我很满意，因为演起来太有趣了。

1441
00:56:18.610 --> 00:56:21.290
And it was unexpected and unpredictable.
而且它出人意料，难以预测。

1442
00:56:21.590 --> 00:56:22.910
And it surprised me.
它让我感到惊喜。

1443
00:56:23.010 --> 00:56:24.350
It surprised the other cast members.
也让其他演员感到惊喜。

1444
00:56:24.410 --> 00:56:25.710
And it was fun to do.
演起来很有趣。

1445
00:56:25.810 --> 00:56:27.270
And it's always nice because he keeps it fresh.
这总是很好，因为他让剧情保持新鲜感。

1446
00:56:27.410 --> 00:56:27.690
Absolutely.
绝对是这样。

1447
00:56:28.230 --> 00:56:28.590
He keeps it fresh, yeah.
他让剧情保持新鲜感，没错。

1448
00:56:28.910 --> 00:56:30.510
You know, get to stretch your acting chops.
你知道，这能让你磨练演技。

1449
00:56:30.910 --> 00:56:34.090
You guys actually stick to the script more than we assume you do, right?
你们实际上比我们想象的更忠于剧本，对吧？

1450
00:56:35.110 --> 00:56:37.110
Well, usually we lay the script out.
嗯，通常我们会先把剧本定下来。

1451
00:56:37.210 --> 00:56:39.370
It depends on the director and his style of directing.
这取决于导演以及他的执导风格。

1452
00:56:39.370 --> 00:56:42.270
But they would like for us to lay it down as written.
但他们希望我们先按剧本原样演出来。

1453
00:56:42.290 --> 00:56:44.310
And then they say, okay, play with it.
然后他们会说，好了，现在可以自由发挥了。

1454
00:56:44.410 --> 00:56:45.390
And then we're allowed to.
接着我们就可以那样做了。

1455
00:56:45.390 --> 00:56:49.690
And then it goes places you never dreamed of.
然后剧情就会走向你意想不到的方向。

1456
00:56:49.710 --> 00:56:51.030
Don't you see any deleted scenes?
你没看到什么删减片段吗？

1457
00:56:52.710 --> 00:56:54.130
Oh, I loved that.
哦，我超喜欢那个。

1458
00:56:54.410 --> 00:56:57.810
You got to share that, Angela, so that people can watch the whole thing.
安吉拉，你得分享出来，这样大家才能看到完整版。

1459
00:56:58.030 --> 00:56:59.510
That was just a little snippet.
那只是个小片段而已。

1460
00:56:59.650 --> 00:57:00.130
I will.
我会的。

1461
00:57:00.230 --> 00:57:03.010
I think I just love that you hear Leslie's laugh.
我觉得我特别喜欢能听到莱斯利的笑声。

1462
00:57:03.210 --> 00:57:06.990
And, you know, he's just full of joy and so not like his Stanley character.
而且，你知道，他本人充满活力，和他在剧中饰演的斯坦利完全不同。

1463
00:57:06.990 --> 00:57:08.450
And I thought it was nice to hear that.
我觉得能听到那个挺好的。

1464
00:57:08.450 --> 00:57:11.290
Well, Phyllis reminded me of another thing about Leslie.
菲利斯提醒了我关于莱斯利的另一件事。

1465
00:57:11.630 --> 00:57:20.090
She said whenever they were at a work party and he would meet someone for the first time without missing a beat, if he saw them at the next work party,
她说每当他们参加公司聚会，他第一次见到某人时，如果下次聚会再见到对方，他总能不假思索地叫出对方的名字。

1466
00:57:20.230 --> 00:57:21.330
he could remember their name.
他能记住他们的名字。

1467
00:57:22.390 --> 00:57:23.350
That's amazing.
太厉害了。

1468
00:57:23.630 --> 00:57:23.930
Yes.
是的。

1469
00:57:24.090 --> 00:57:24.770
That's a talent.
那真是一种天赋。

1470
00:57:25.550 --> 00:57:27.090
I remember that about him.
关于他这一点，我记得。

1471
00:57:27.370 --> 00:57:32.710
It was pretty incredible, actually, because we would meet a lot of people at those events.
其实真的很不可思议，因为我们在那些活动上会见到很多人。

1472
00:57:32.990 --> 00:57:34.770
And he would remember everybody.
但他能记住每一个人。

1473
00:57:35.330 --> 00:57:35.510
Yeah.
没错。

1474
00:57:35.510 --> 00:57:38.070
Well, all right, everyone, we're getting to the end here.
好了，各位，我们快要结束了。

1475
00:57:38.190 --> 00:57:40.150
But we did get a fan question from Matt T.
但我们收到了一条来自密歇根州艾伦代尔的马特·T的粉丝提问。

1476
00:57:40.330 --> 00:57:47.570
in Allendale, Michigan, who said, do we know how many crossword puzzles Leslie slash Stanley worked on over the years?
他问，我们知不知道莱斯利，也就是斯坦利，这些年来做了多少填字游戏？

1477
00:57:48.690 --> 00:57:55.110
Well, first of all, Leslie said he really did do the crossword puzzles and he did lots of them.
首先，莱斯利说他确实做了填字游戏，而且做了很多。

1478
00:57:55.110 --> 00:57:55.790
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1479
00:57:56.310 --> 00:57:56.890
Yes.
是的。

1480
00:57:57.110 --> 00:58:00.530
One time he was asked this and he sort of did the math.
有一次有人问他这个问题，他大概算了一下。

1481
00:58:00.690 --> 00:58:10.230
He said, OK, over a nine-year period, about five a year, over, hmm, I think 60 books we went through.
他说，好吧，在九年时间里，一年大约做五个，一共做了，嗯，我想我们用了60本书。

1482
00:58:11.390 --> 00:58:13.890
Sixty books of crossword puzzles.
六十本填字游戏书。

1483
00:58:14.010 --> 00:58:14.060
That's what he said.
他是这么说的。

1484
00:58:14.060 --> 00:58:14.470
That's what he said.
他是这么说的。

1485
00:58:15.870 --> 00:58:22.170
Well, Leslie also shared that he actually fell asleep at his desk, just like Stanley did.
莱斯利还分享说，他确实在办公桌前睡着过，就像斯坦利一样。

1486
00:58:22.730 --> 00:58:26.590
I mean, can you blame him coming in at five in the morning, sitting back there?
我是说，你能怪他吗？凌晨五点就来上班，坐在后面。

1487
00:58:26.770 --> 00:58:30.570
He said when he had the mask on for the Halloween episode, he fell asleep.
他说拍万圣节那集戴着面具的时候，他睡着了。

1488
00:58:31.190 --> 00:58:35.070
And also once after a Christmas party, he fell asleep on the couch.
还有一次圣诞派对后，他在沙发上睡着了。

1489
00:58:36.110 --> 00:58:37.470
I kind of remember that.
我好像记得那件事。

1490
00:58:37.590 --> 00:58:38.050
I do, too.
我也记得。

1491
00:58:38.210 --> 00:58:38.410
Yeah.
没错。

1492
00:58:39.090 --> 00:58:41.390
We just tiptoed around him while he knapsed.
我们就在他打盹的时候蹑手蹑脚地绕过他。

1493
00:58:41.390 --> 00:58:42.230
I remember that.
我记得那件事。

1494
00:58:42.230 --> 00:58:42.610
I do, too.
我也记得。

1495
00:58:42.690 --> 00:58:43.370
I remember that.
我记得那件事。

1496
00:58:44.570 --> 00:58:49.750
Well, you know, as we talk about the character Stanley, I always love to know what episodes
你知道，当我们谈论斯坦利这个角色时，我总是很想知道我们的演员伙伴们

1497
00:58:49.750 --> 00:58:54.870
or scenes our castmates hold dear or have great memories of their time filming The Office.
最珍视哪些剧集或场景，或者对他们拍摄《办公室》的时光有什么美好的回忆。

1498
00:58:55.130 --> 00:59:01.150
And Leslie said his favorite Stanley-focused scene was when Michael Scott tried reviving
莱斯利说他最喜欢的以斯坦利为中心的场景是迈克尔·斯科特试图抢救

1499
00:59:01.150 --> 00:59:02.810
Stanley from his heart attack.
心脏病发作的斯坦利的那一段。

1500
00:59:03.250 --> 00:59:03.850
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1501
00:59:03.950 --> 00:59:08.750
And his favorite non-focused Stanley episode was Phyllis and Bob Vance's wedding.
他最喜欢的非焦点斯坦利剧集是菲利斯和鲍勃·万斯的婚礼那一集。

1502
00:59:09.110 --> 00:59:09.550
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1503
00:59:09.550 --> 00:59:14.730
He said he also really enjoyed the episode where Dwight and Clark roll him in bubble wrap.
他说他也非常喜欢德怀特和克拉克把他裹进气泡膜里的那一集。

1504
00:59:14.970 --> 00:59:17.930
Yes, he talked about that in his Staramageddon interview.
没错，他在“星际末日”采访中也提到了这一点。

1505
00:59:18.190 --> 00:59:18.610
He did.
确实。

1506
00:59:18.730 --> 00:59:22.070
And then we talked to Clark, and it was also one of his favorite episodes.
然后我们和克拉克聊了聊，那也是他最喜欢的剧集之一。

1507
00:59:22.990 --> 00:59:26.870
Finally, I thought we could end with Stanley's Where Are They Now?
最后，我想我们可以以“斯坦利现在在哪里？”作为结尾。

1508
00:59:27.590 --> 00:59:30.770
You know, there's a lot of theories about where each of the characters are.
你知道，关于每个角色现在的去向有很多理论。

1509
00:59:30.990 --> 00:59:31.250
Yes.
是的。

1510
00:59:31.250 --> 00:59:35.970
And pretty unanimously, everyone thinks Stanley's very happy in Florida.
而且几乎一致认为，大家都觉得斯坦利在佛罗里达过得很开心。

1511
00:59:36.230 --> 00:59:36.610
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1512
00:59:36.770 --> 00:59:39.510
And I think Stanley answers it the best in the finale.
我觉得斯坦利在结局里回答得最好。

1513
00:59:39.850 --> 00:59:46.190
He says, yes, I'm living in Florida now, a little town called Florida City, just on the
他说，是的，我现在住在佛罗里达，一个小镇叫佛罗里达城，就在

1514
00:59:46.190 --> 00:59:47.290
edge of the Everglades.
大沼泽地的边缘。

1515
00:59:47.470 --> 00:59:51.750
The man who delivered my divorce papers came by fan boat, which was kind of fun.
给我送离婚协议书的那个人是坐气垫船来的，还挺有意思的。

1516
00:59:51.970 --> 00:59:54.750
I sit on my porch all day carving birds.
我整天坐在门廊上雕刻鸟儿。

1517
00:59:55.410 --> 00:59:56.750
Well, there you have it.
好吧，就是这样。

1518
00:59:56.890 --> 01:00:00.450
That's all about Stanley Hudson in honor of Pretzel Day this Saturday.
这就是关于斯坦利·哈德森的一切，以此纪念本周六的椒盐卷饼日。

1519
01:00:00.690 --> 01:00:03.070
Make sure you get yourself some free pretzels.
一定要去给自己领些免费的椒盐卷饼。

1520
01:00:03.210 --> 01:00:04.430
It'll mean you're laid back.
那意味着你很悠闲。

1521
01:00:04.710 --> 01:00:05.430
That's right.
没错。

1522
01:00:05.710 --> 01:00:07.010
Have a laid back Saturday.
祝大家周六过得悠闲自在。

1523
01:00:07.430 --> 01:00:07.910
We'll be back Saturday.
我们周六会回来。

1524
01:00:08.430 --> 01:00:10.070
Thanks so much for writing in, you guys.
非常感谢你们的来信。

1525
01:00:10.230 --> 01:00:14.510
And thanks so much to Leslie for telling us about his audition and sharing with us about
也非常感谢莱斯利告诉我们他的试镜经历，并与我们分享了

1526
01:00:14.510 --> 01:00:15.350
his time on the show.
他在剧组的那段时光。

1527
01:00:15.510 --> 01:00:17.550
We love you guys, and we hope you have a good one.
我们爱你们，希望你们过得愉快。

1528
01:00:17.670 --> 01:00:18.450
See you next time.
下次见。

1529
01:00:18.450 --> 01:00:28.860
